WEBVTT

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.290
Sorry about this. Rin-chan already left the studio,

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:11.920
and lchigo-chan is on her way,
so please wait a little longer.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.970
Okay, I understand.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:17.970
The two of them are so busy.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.720
Oh, good work today!

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:20.860
Good work today!

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:26.250
lchinose-san, you've got a job!
As a program-reg on a new anime!

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.920
Self-care

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.320
A program-reg! I'm so happy!

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:07.910
Program-reg is short for 'program regular."

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:09.490
This doesn't refer to a specific role,

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:15.110
but each episode, program regulars
play bit parts with only a few lines-koro.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:18.250
On top of that, the main character
will be played by Shiraishi Ryoko-san!

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:23.550
Shiraishi-san is also the main character
of the butler anime I love!

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.050
First is episode one!

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:28.870
My character is Boy A, who picks
a fight with the Western Detective.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:33.260
A boy's voice, huh?

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:37.580
You bastard...!

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:41.890
In order to keep from disturbing the neighbors,
muffle your voice with a pillow-koro.
You bastard...!

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:49.500
I wonder if I should use a lower voice...?

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:52.520
I finally got work. I have to do well!

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:55.500
You bastard...!

00:02:55.500 --> 00:03:00.500
You little! What the hell?!

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:08.290
I thought I was gonna die...

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.790
You have to remember to breathe-koro!

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:14.310
I... I think I got a little too into it.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.400
Good morning!
Western Detective
Episode 1 Recording

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.190
Good morning!

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:25.690
I'm Ichinose Futaba from Aozora Production.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:27.820
I look forward to working with you today.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:29.310
I do, too.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.160
Good morning!

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:33.740
Good morning!

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:38.440
It's Shiraishi Ryoko-san!

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.450
Oh, good morning!

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.420
Good morning.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.030
Sh-She's so pretty!

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:57.350
So, Detective Macaroni is the main character,
so we want him to sound kind of heroic.

00:03:57.350 --> 00:04:00.010
Heroic... Is he passionate?

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:05.890
No, he looks funny, but he's actually handsome,
so he should be a little sexy, too.

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:08.530
"Pasta is Macaroni Western!"

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:09.440
Like that?

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:11.860
Your gender's different now!

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:17.650
All right. "Pasta is Macaroni Western!"

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:19.830
Does that work?

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:21.150
Yeah, that's good.

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:24.650
Oh, she can do anything!

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:27.460
A handsome man, or a woman...

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:30.160
It's wonderful that she can
do all sorts of characters!

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:31.800
I, too...

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:35.680
We'll do the walla all together at the end.

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:38.430
So, l'm counting on you
to do it like I just explained.

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:39.950
Okay!

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:45.470
Oh, that's right.
This part where I talk to Shiraishi-san...

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:47.180
The other day, when I went to an event...

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:47.960
Yeah?

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:49.440
There was a typhoon!

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:50.810
On top of that, it was an outdoor performance!

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:52.580
Really, what happened?!

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:53.820
It was cancelled, of course.

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:55.700
Excuse me, Shiraishi-san?

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:56.350
Yes?

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:59.160
In cut 62...

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:00.860
Let's see, 62...

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:04.320
Handsome!
Like a hero!
Bang!

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.080
I-I see.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:08.040
Even though she's pretty,
she has that side of her, too,

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.250
which is why she can do male voices so easily...

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:15.090
Stop right there!

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:18.140
Even if you steal that, you won't be able to
use it if you don't go through the cash register!

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.310
Whoa, wait right there!

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:23.670
I won't let you get past me.

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:26.760
Wow... It's a cool voice,
just like the director said.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:28.440
Who're you?!

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:32.030
Pasta is Macaroni Western!

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:36.370
The unforgiven one from the West,
the Western Detective...

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:37.610
"Western Detective"

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:38.820
...is me!
"Western Detective"

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:39.430
...is me!

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:42.460
Bring it on, you bastard-

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.630
Hey, are you all right, Boy A?

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:51.300
l'm sorry!

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:54.630
She's serious from the dry run. Ah, to be young.

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:57.830
Give us a break. Now we can't slack off.

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:00.300
Are you all right?

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:03.840
Yes. Sorry to stop everything.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.690
Okay, let's try again from cut 56.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:10.520
Bring it on, you bastard!

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:15.110
Good work today!

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.280
Good work today!

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:21.990
Looks like your throat isn't doing too well.

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:24.870
Oh, yes. Sorry about that.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:27.040
Ginger tea is good for times like that.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.650
No, you should use a propolis throat spray!

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:31.380
First, you should use a neck warmer-

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:32.820
Manuka honey is good, too.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:39.010
I put as many cough drops as I can in my mouth,
put a face mask on, and go to sleep.

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:40.720
My record is four!

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:42.920
That won't kill me?

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:46.310
Be careful. Feel better!

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:48.520
Well, good work today!

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:50.060
Good work today!

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:06.370
The sound director said it was okay,
but was it really okay?

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:09.440
Boy A might appear in a later episode, too.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:11.880
I have to get a lot better at it!

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:19.290
I'm dizzy from being in the bath for too long...

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:23.930
I shouldn't practice too much in the bath...

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:29.890
What? Ichinose-san has a cold?

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:30.790
I'm sorry.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:41.810
Yes, it looks like you can do
this week's recording separately.

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:45.580
First, you need to devote
yourself to getting better.

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:46.620
Yes, ma'am.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:49.820
Also, I think you already know this, but...

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:51.310
Yes.

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:54.420
I will be careful from now on...

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:55.520
I'm sorry...

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:03.930
When I try my best not to be left behind
by the other two, this is what happens...

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.640
I have to get better fast!

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:11.940
I have to get back to the studio soon!

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.980
Western Detective
Episode 3 Recording

00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:18.310
I apologize for last week!

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:19.780
It's fine, it's fine.

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:21.280
More importantly, are you okay?

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:23.360
Yes! I'm fine now.

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:25.560
Good morning!

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:26.680
Oh, Shiraishi-san!

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:30.040
Sorry to cause you trouble last week.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:32.790
It's okay. Sounds like you had a rough time.

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:36.520
Oh, right. Here are some more cough drops.

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:38.620
I thought you might've run out.

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:40.460
I can have these?

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:42.010
Thank you very much!

00:08:42.010 --> 00:08:43.870
I'm counting on you today, too, Futaba-chan.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:46.750
Right! I look forward to working with you today!

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:59.650
Good work!

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:01.240
Good work today!

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:04.160
Oh? Are you going this way, too, Futaba-chan?

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:05.990
Let's go home together.

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:06.830
Okay!

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:16.210
Um, thanks so much for the cough drops!

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:20.210
Don't worry about it. I have a ton stocked up.

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:24.010
By the way, Futaba-chan, you're in
a unit called Earphones, right?

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:27.300
Oh, yes, that's right.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:31.250
I've been in one before, too.
Units are fun, aren't they?

00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:36.420
But, there's a big difference
between me and the other members...

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:42.490
I have to work hard so I don't drag them down!

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:45.570
I see. So that's why you
were overdoing it a little.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:53.320
I think it was when I was just
around your age that I hurt my throat.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:57.320
It wasn't a cold. I had something
called vocal cord nodules.

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:01.550
It would have been fine
if I just rested properly,

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:03.840
but it was just when I was starting to get busy,

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:07.220
and above all, work was fun,
so I pushed myself a little too much...

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:08.830
So it got worse.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:11.220
And then,

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:12.770
I had surgery on my throat.

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:19.730
There weren't really any seiyuu who had gotten
the surgery before around me at the time...

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:22.860
It'd be a lie if I said I wasn't uneasy.

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:26.810
Even so, you had the surgery?

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:29.160
Yeah. I mean...

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:35.080
I want to work as a seiyuu
for the rest of my life.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:41.840
Oh, yeah. You can get those
cough drops online, too...

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:44.130
Let's see... Here's the website...

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:48.090
Huh?! Why are you crying?!

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:51.210
D-Don't worry! You only had a cold!

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.470
You won't have to get surgery!

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:56.930
I'm sorry... I'm fine... Sorry...

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:10.730
That wasn't it, Shiraishi-san. I wasn't crying
because I was afraid I'd have to get surgery...

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:14.230
I was crying because I'd
remembered something important.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:18.230
I was impatient because there was a
difference between me and my friends,

00:11:18.230 --> 00:11:21.420
but to me, this is work
I want to do for a lifetime...

00:11:22.270 --> 00:11:24.240
That's what being a seiyuu is.

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:27.670
There may be times when there is a
difference between me and the others.

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:31.210
Even so, I will go at my own pace...

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:35.010
Hello?

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:36.840
Hey, Futaba! Big news!

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:40.840
We're putting on a concert!
Earphones' first solo concert!

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:42.810
What? Our first concert?

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:49.120
That's right! And Kaibara-san booked
an amazing place for it, as usual!

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:52.620
Oh, Rin-chan's calling me, too.

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:55.700
Oh, yeah! Anyway, let's do our best!

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:58.360
Together, the three of us!

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:06.410
Earphones is finally having its first concert!

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:09.910
And the first week ticket sales are...

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:12.000
In a hall that can seat 500...

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:14.500
We've sold 12 tickets...

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:18.630
Why did I get a place that
could seat 500 people, I wonder...?

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.420
You shouldn't be talking!

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:24.090
It's fine. We've still got time.
Let's do our best.

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:25.930
Yeah, that's right. We just have to do it!

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:28.560
Anyway, we have to advertise!

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:30.600
On the radio, of course, but also on our blog.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:34.940
I'll also ask to see if they'll write
about it when I'm in magazines.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:39.900
I'll... um... practice my
singing and dancing more

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:42.860
and work hard so the people
who come will have a good time!

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:47.660
I'll try to see if other radio shows
will have you on as guests!

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:52.450
There's a lot to do before the concert,
so we don't have time to be depressed!

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:54.710
Yeah, you're right.

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:59.760
Okay, great, that's the spirit.
I feel better now.

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:02.710
And, there's something else
I want to talk to you three about.

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:04.340
What will you do at the concert?

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:07.760
What do you mean, what will we do...?

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:11.930
Hm? I mean, you guys don't have
enough songs for a full concert.

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:17.440
You only have three songs: "lnto Your Ears,"
and the radio opening and ending songs.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:20.270
That's only enough for a mini concert.

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:22.030
<i>You're</i> the one who decided
we were doing a concert!

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:25.320
Isn't that something you think about
with the producer beforehand?!

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:27.820
Why are you so irresponsible?!

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:31.290
We can't actually say any
of these things out loud, though.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:33.460
What's wrong? You're shaking.

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:34.870
Are you nervous?

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:38.830
Don't worry, don't worry. I brought some ideas.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:40.340
Ideas?

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:43.050
That's right! Idea number one!

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:45.470
We'll do a public recording of the radio show!

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:48.890
Idea two! We'll have game and present segments!

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:51.100
Idea three! We can increase the number
of songs by having you sing covers!

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:52.640
Covers?

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:55.600
Yeah, but you probably don't want to do that

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:59.810
because you'll have to learn the songs and
dances for them all between now and the concert.

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:04.240
For a two-hour concert, it'll be a lot of songs.

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:06.200
Then, we'll have to do...

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:08.320
Game segments and things...?

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:10.020
I want to do the cover songs.

00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:13.790
It's our first concert!

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:17.040
I want to work hard at singing and dancing
rather than doing a game segment!

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:21.670
I want to charm the audience
with our singing! With our dancing!

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:25.300
But in that case, because of the budget,

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:28.340
you'll have to come up with
the choreography by yourselves...

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:31.970
It's fine! I'll do all of it!

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:35.020
But I don't know if we'll
be able to do it or not...

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:37.850
You can't give up already, Rin-chan! Futaba!

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:39.850
If you give up-

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:42.360
Then the game is over!

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:44.860
This isn't a game, though.

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:46.740
1st Solo Concert!
EARPHONES

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:47.400
EARPHONES
1st Solo Concert!

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:49.950
Sidestep!

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:51.220
Right!

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:51.930
Left!

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:53.390
Right?

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:54.080
Left?

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:56.660
Hey, you doing the robot dance over there.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:57.830
That's not what I'm doing!

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.920
How can you mess up that much?

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.670
I told you what to do, didn't I?

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:07.670
Sorry, I remember the choreography,
but my body can't keep up...

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:11.430
Hm... Are the steps too complicated?

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:14.390
Let's see... then...

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:18.180
One more time! Wait, I don't think
one more time will be enough,

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:21.100
but let me try again with the same choreography!

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:25.190
I will definitely master the dance
you came up with, Ichigo!

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.550
Futaba...

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:30.360
All right! Nothing less from
a member of Earphones!

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:32.320
You can do it, Futaba-san!

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:34.320
Yeah!

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:45.380
Now, we have to decide
the rest of the cover songs today!

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:49.340
Uh... There's more stuff to learn...

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:53.430
Oh, if it's a song from <i>Ikinone Korori</i>,
then I might remember the lyrics.

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:56.010
We can't do a song that no one knows!

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:57.970
Then, what about the opening
of that butler anime?

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:00.890
That's such a major song that
we'll just sound like a bad copy!

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:03.480
Then, I want to do "Give Me Wings"-

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:04.900
This isn't a choral competition!

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:07.610
We have to think about this more strategically!

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:09.740
First, we should calculate
the average age of the audience

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:12.450
based on listener mail sent to the radio show.

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:15.030
We can use that as a basis
for guessing what they like.

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:17.330
We'll make sure to cover the
standard transforming girl shows,

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:19.870
passionate mecha shows,
have some tearful ballads...

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:24.040
Oh, and we can't forget the strange and catchy
denpa songs that are sure to fire things up!

00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:30.550
Don't underestimate me, whose
music player is filled with anime songs!

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:32.010
lchigo-san has...

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:33.590
...awakened or something!

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:37.970
Right now, I'll make you listen
to my best selection nonstop!

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:41.770
Learn the trends with your body!

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:45.770
Right. Right. Well, goodbye.

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:49.730
By the way, my best selection has 80 volumes!

00:16:49.730 --> 00:16:51.480
What...?

00:16:54.920 --> 00:16:57.120
My whole body hurts...

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:03.560
Good work~
Good work today!

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:03.710
Good work~

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:07.560
My whole body
is sore~
Good work~

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:07.670
My whole body
is sore~

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:12.570
How pathetic-
My whole body
is sore~

00:17:12.570 --> 00:17:12.720
How pathetic-

00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:16.680
We're working hard every day, so it can't be
helped~ Rin-chan, you're sore, too, aren't you?

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:19.470
Yeah~ It'll be better once I
sleep though, since I'm young~

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:22.500
l'm young, too!
l'm young, too!

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:23.160
Yeah~ It'll be better once I
sleep though, since I'm young~

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:25.400
Sorry, I just remembered
something I have to do!

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:26.140
Me too!

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:29.150
I wonder what's wrong, all of a sudden?

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:33.650
It doesn't hurt! It doesn't hurt! I'm still-

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:37.200
I'm still young enough to get rid
of muscle soreness after a day-

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.680
Ow!

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:41.000
Ow....!

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:44.370
52 tickets, you said...?

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:50.380
That's right. Currently, 52 tickets
have sold for the Earphones concert.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:53.800
For a hall that can seat 500 people,
we've sold 52...

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:56.180
We finally sold fifty?

00:17:56.180 --> 00:17:58.050
They seem to be selling slowly but steadily.

00:17:58.050 --> 00:18:00.640
It's the result of us
persistently promoting it, isn't it?

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:05.140
All right! Let's keep at it so even more
people will know about the concert!

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:06.440
Okay!

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:09.060
Your optimism is great!

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:10.570
All right, I've got it!

00:18:10.570 --> 00:18:13.570
l'll exert myself and pull out
something amazing, too!

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:15.570
This! The Anison Autumn Festival,
or Anitumn for short!

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:19.530
The Anison Autumn Festival,
or Anitumn for short!

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:22.330
The super major event featuring
popular artists all in one place!

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:24.330
If you promote the concert at this event,

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:27.790
you'll definitely raise
awareness about the concert!

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:31.000
No way, Anitumn?!

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.750
Even I've heard of it before!

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:36.090
We'll be able to promote
our concert at that huge venue?

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:39.140
Will you do it?

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:43.100
Of course we will! We can't refuse that-

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:46.850
Oh no! What'll I do? I'm super excited now!

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:48.230
M-M-Me too!

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:50.350
I'm so happy my heart's pounding!

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:03.820
Welcome to the Anison Autumn Festival!

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:07.960
Earphones is having a concert...

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:10.880
It's our first concert... Please support us...

00:19:10.880 --> 00:19:12.330
Please support us...!

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:17.170
Wow, as expected of Anitumn.
It's really popular.

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:19.550
By "promote," you meant
we were passing out flyers?!

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:21.110
On top of that, we're outside the venue!

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:24.870
Even if it was impossible for us to sing,
I thought we'd at least get to go on stage!

00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:28.980
We're Earphones! Please support us!

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:32.730
Please support us!

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:35.690
We're Earphones! Please support us!

00:19:39.090 --> 00:19:40.660
It's so cold...

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:41.450
Here.

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:45.450
It's the stick-on kind, so you
can put it on under your clothes.

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:47.160
Please support us!
You're very prepared.

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:48.040
Self care is part of our job, too!
Please support us!

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:49.790
Please come!
Self care is part of our job, too!

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:52.000
Please support us!

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:53.560
Please come!

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:55.170
Please support us!

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:57.290
Please come!

00:19:58.940 --> 00:20:01.840
It feels like a school festival! It's fun!

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:05.720
That's true. There's something nice
about handing it to people directly.

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:11.560
You guys are too positive, too carefree!

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:12.880
lt's fine to be carefree, don't you think?

00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:13.350
We're Earphones!

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:13.960
l'm sure this is just our pace. Yeah!

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:15.740
Please come!

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:17.860
l'm sure this is just our pace. Yeah!

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:23.070
All right, just a little bit left!

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:24.950
Let's give them all out!

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:25.870
Roger!

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:32.670
We're Earphones! Please support us!
It's our first concert!

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:37.500
Okay then, we're going to start!

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:43.470
All right, that looks like the last of them.

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:46.140
Yes. Everyone, we're going!

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:47.410
Okay!

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:51.940
Next, it's our turn.

00:20:51.940 --> 00:20:52.920
Yeah.

00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:01.110
I got an email from Kaibara-san.

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:04.740
He says 200 tickets were sold.

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:07.740
Two hundred? Really?

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:10.640
That's amazing!
It went up all at once, didn't it?

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:12.460
Of course.

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:14.790
Yes, thank you!

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:16.080
We'll do our best!

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:19.800
Looks like it'll work out somehow.

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:21.460
I'm so glad.

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:26.340
Yes, and we've decided on the cover songs
and finished most of the choreography, too!

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:28.560
It feels like we're almost ready, doesn't it?

00:21:28.560 --> 00:21:29.600
Yeah, well.

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:33.940
Wait, it's not like all the seats have been sold!
This is no time to be celebrating !

00:21:33.940 --> 00:21:35.600
Come on, practice! Practice!

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:37.100
Okay.

00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:39.480
Today, we'll do the last phrase-

00:21:44.610 --> 00:21:45.440
Ichigo?!

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:47.320
lchigo-san!

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:48.580
Are you all right?

00:21:49.510 --> 00:21:51.660
Ow... I'm fine. This is nothing.

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:54.120
Jeez, you guys are overreacting.

00:22:30.970 --> 00:22:33.410
Okay, Earphones is finally having a solo concert!

00:22:33.410 --> 00:22:34.100
Yay!

00:22:34.100 --> 00:22:36.580
So, let's make an acrostic poem
with the "solo"!

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:37.460
O-Okay...!

00:22:37.460 --> 00:22:38.420
Let's start with "S"!

00:22:38.420 --> 00:22:40.000
Um... Soulfully!

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:40.350
"O"!

00:22:40.350 --> 00:22:41.750
"O"? One-step, two-step, dance?!

00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:42.220
"L"!

00:22:42.220 --> 00:22:43.180
Lively and dramatically!

00:22:43.180 --> 00:22:43.570
"O"!

00:22:43.570 --> 00:22:44.840
O... Outdoor garden!

00:22:44.840 --> 00:22:46.140
Why'd you choose that?!

00:22:46.140 --> 00:22:49.090
arayuru kea wa nyuunen ni
We have to take good care of ourselves

00:22:49.090 --> 00:22:53.350
isshou yaritai shigoto dakara
Because we want to do this job for a long time

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:56.730
itsudatte karada ga shihon desu
Our bodies are our precious assets!

00:22:56.730 --> 00:22:58.700
Now, we have a request!

00:22:58.700 --> 00:23:02.180
From <i>Mahou Sensei Negima,</i>
it's "Happy Material"!

00:23:02.180 --> 00:23:05.520
hikaru kaze wo oikoshitara
Once I overtake the glittering wind,

00:23:05.520 --> 00:23:08.400
kimi ni kitto aeru ne
I'm sure I'll meet you

00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:14.410
atarashii kagayaki happy ready go!!
A new brilliance, Happy Ready Go!!

00:23:16.180 --> 00:23:18.410
Yay! Let's keep this energy up!

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:19.750
Ready, go!
